<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;"><strong>An apparent honeytrap scandal invo=
lving the boss of the world=E2=80=99s most valuable company</strong> and a =
suspected Chinese spy is rocking the AI sector. Overnight, Nvidia announced=
 it is launching an independent investigation amid reports that founder and=
 CEO Jensen Huang has been the target of =E2=80=9Ca foreign intelligence ef=
fort=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">That effort, reports claim, led to Huang i=
nto a romantic relationship with a Chinese woman, <strong>Alice Huang</stro=
ng>, who was recruited to spy for China=E2=80=99s Ministry of State Securit=
y intelligence agency.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Last night, <strong>Jensen</strong> <stron=
g>Huang</strong> admitted having an affair, telling Nvidia staff: =E2=80=9C=
I owe my family and all of you an apology. I was unfaithful to my wife. My =
actions hurt her and our children. There is no excuse for what I did. I am =
deeply sorry.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The issue goes much further than simply a =
CEO=E2=80=99s conduct. It falls squarely within US concerns it could lose t=
he AI race to China. Alice Huang worked for a Singapore-based datacentre fi=
rm called Megaspeed, suspected of routing Nvidia chips to China and evading=
 export controls.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Jensen Huang has been a critic of those re=
strictions, arguing in May 2025 that US export controls designed to limit C=
hina=E2=80=99s access to AI chips were a =E2=80=9Ca failure=E2=80=9D, and h=
ad simply encouraged China to develop its own alternatives.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The revelation comes just a few days after=
 shares in AI-linked companies tumbled, before a late recovery on Wall Stre=
et on Friday. Today, Asia-Pacific markets are staging a recovery =E2=80=93 =
Japan=E2=80=99s Nikkei has jumped by 2.2%, while Taiwan=E2=80=99s TAIEX has=
 surged almost 5%. South Korea=E2=80=99s Kospi is missing out, though, down=
 by 0.6%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Nvidia=E2=80=99s investigation introduces =
more uncertainty for semiconductor stocks and the broader AI investment eco=
system, says Naeem Aslam, CIO of Zaye Capital Markets: =E2=80=9CEuropean te=
ch manufacturers and semiconductor equipment suppliers remain particularly =
exposed to developments in American AI spending, meaning any renewed sellin=
g pressure on Wall Street could quickly spread across European equity marke=
ts.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Bloomberg say the scandal is a =E2=80=9Chu=
mbling moment=E2=80=9D for Huang, calling him one of Silicon Valley=E2=80=
=99s biggest celebrities in recent years. Bill Ackman, CEO of investment fi=
rm Pershing Square, is hoping that Jensen Huang=E2=80=99s dalliance is mere=
ly a =E2=80=98simple affair=E2=80=99, not a national security threat. While=
 Donald Trump told reporters: =E2=80=9CI have not spoken to him about it. I=
 just know he=E2=80=99s a fine person, but you never know what is going on.=
 I hope everything=E2=80=99s fine ... I think he=E2=80=99s an honourable gu=
y.=E2=80=9C</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A Chinese state-run newspaper has denied B=
eijing had any link to <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/=
ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBUsSd6DY9A_zGHjXnJyBTsj=
fyKRnviVI97-dF2T9L5KUIenkDeiOsVRb9zSV4wK7b1sSmE9QyrlIsO2HGz6kwd8bzzSVJjOgrC=
s33R0WOMhQtf_usP3S-jjrKeS43lDp7P38VK4HZ7cIjVwPcWYQAo7BCMzfd7HmwnhMms3JLLSO0=
Eaxv7E12NJyp8QwWfMQw/4vl/i7h1-4s9QB2dZeEPZyhquw/h29/h001.1vAB7oJVbPB1t55_Xs=
RYUV5rVUl47A3k5jDdz9cl_3o" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Nvidia</a> CEO Jensen =
Huang=E2=80=99s extramarital affair. The Global Times, a nationalist tabloi=
d, said American outlets, in particular the New York Times, were =E2=80=9Cg=
oing crazy=E2=80=9D with speculative stories.</p>
